From f65044b04982b50df705fc22cd1432b5fb80f92f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:02:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): the lathe posts state G97 before a section that is
 not constant surface speed

A section that posted G96 now cancels it at its end: a bare G97 right
after the main spindle stop (M05 / M5), before any after-operation word.
Every following section - a C-axis live-tool section, a drill on centre,
a thread, a tap, a probe, a speed-0 section - opens under constant rpm
unless it states G96 itself, and no program ends in CSS mode. Before,
a live-tool section after a CSS turning section on the Fanuc lathe post
started its live spindle (M1003 S3000) with G96 still modal, so its S
could be read as a surface speed.

Both lathe posts (fanuc-lathe.cps, tormach-lathe.cps) take the rule; no
other shipped post writes G96. The clamp logic, the per-rev feed words
and every program with no G96 section are unchanged; the only golden
that changes is nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc (one G97 after its M05).

Pinned by lathe_post_refusals (live-tool, thread and drill twins, two
CSS sections in a row), lathe_post_tormach (the drill twin, two CSS
sections), and the new recorded case css_then_live in every per-post
script suite (fanuc-lathe posts it; every other post refuses the C
section by name), on a test-bench mill-turn fixture with placeholder
live-tool words.

Fixes #1173

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
